  "id": "Compound::DB00695 - Gene::760",
  "verbalization": "Furosemide's interaction with Ca2 is supported by multiple pathways that converge on a shared mechanism involving Ca14 and Ca7. The drug binds to Ca14, which then participates in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide, an activity that is also participated by Ca2. This suggests a potential link between Furosemide and Ca2 through a chain of enzymatic and ionic interactions. The evidence indicates that Ca2 may be indirectly involved in the metabolic processes influenced by Furosemide, though the exact nature of this involvement remains unclear. The overlapping participation of Ca14 and Ca7 in different biochemical pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, and further studies would be needed to elucidate the precise molecular mechanism linking Furosemide to Ca2.",
